# BizMate AI Data Model
Version: 1.0
Status: Approved
Last Updated: 2026-07-26

---

# 1. Purpose

This document defines the logical data model for BizMate AI.

It describes the business entities, their relationships, ownership model, constraints, and data governance rules.

It is independent of any specific database technology. SQL migration files will implement this model.

---

# 2. Data Model Principles

The data model follows these principles:

- UUID primary keys
- Multi-tenant by design
- Business-owned data
- UTC timestamps
- Immutable audit history
- Soft deletes where appropriate
- Referential integrity
- Minimal redundancy
- Future extensibility

---

# 3. Naming Conventions

## Tables

Plural nouns.

Examples:

- businesses
- customers
- products
- sales

---

## Primary Keys

Every table uses:

id

(UUID)

---

## Foreign Keys

Use:

business_id

customer_id

product_id

sale_id

payment_id

expense_id

user_id

---

## Timestamps

created_at

updated_at

deleted_at

All timestamps are stored in UTC.

